title D03e | Persistence port, adapter and transaction lifetime
interface IRepository {
+ begin() : void
+ commit() : void
+ rollback() : void noexcept
+ assignment(id : Id) : Assignment
+ submission(id : Id) : Submission
+ latestVersion(id : Id, withBytes : bool) : SubmissionVersion
+ addSubmission(assignment : Id, student : Id) : Id
+ addVersion(version : const SubmissionVersion&) : void
+ saveSubmission(submission : const Submission&) : void
+ assessment(id : Id) : optional<Assessment>
+ saveAssessment(assessment : const Assessment&) : void
+ addEvent(event : const AssessmentEvent&) : void
+ events(submission : Id) : vector<AssessmentEvent>
+ backup(path : const string&) : void
}
class SqliteRepository {
+ SqliteRepository(path : const string&)
+ ~SqliteRepository()
- db_ : sqlite3*
}
class UnitOfWork {
- repo_ : IRepository&
- committed_ : bool
+ UnitOfWork(repo : IRepository&)
+ ~UnitOfWork()
+ commit() : void
}
SqliteRepository ..|> IRepository : implements all operations
UnitOfWork --> "1" IRepository : borrows
note right of SqliteRepository
Prepared statements and connection cleanup use RAII.
All interface operations are overridden.
Only selected assessment and transaction methods
are expanded here; full contract is Repository.hpp.
end note
note bottom of UnitOfWork
Constructor begins the transaction.
Destructor rolls back unless commit succeeded.
Copy/assignment are deleted.
end note
@enduml
